## VERDICT CANDIDATE

> **DEFECT-WITH-FORMULA, one channel of two.**
>
> Under this project's detection model — deterministic in the *true* parameters
> θ, not in the data (`simulation_detection_probability.py:175-179`) — the MFG
> numerator carries `1[det(θ)]` inside the θ-integral. It leaves the integral
> only for coordinates the analysis *retains*. Therefore:
>
> * **2D channel — correct as implemented, up to a measured residual.** The
>   channel retains `(d_L^obs, M_z^obs)`, the two coordinates `S_4D` acts in.
>   The formally required factor `S_4D(d_L(z;h), M(1+z))` inside `g_i`'s
>   M-integral collapses, at `σ_cond ≈ 8.8e-8`, to `S_4D` evaluated at the
>   **data** — an event-wise constant, h-independent, invisible to the posterior.
>   The omission is a formal one with no numerical consequence. (Residual: the
>   z-quadrature tails, where `d_L(z;h) ≠ d_L,det`. Bounded by measurement M2.)
> * **1D channel — defect.** The channel discards `M_z^obs`, the coordinate whose
>   `(1+z)` lift carries the factor's entire h-dependence. The correct numerator
>   carries `S̄_φ(z;h)` inside the quadrature. Measured magnitude: **+207.0 nats
>   per unit h** summed over 1590 events, 94.7% of events positive, essentially
>   linear over the grid — against a 1D ln-posterior down-tilt of −247.4 (iiib) /
>   −184.0 (joint_r1) nats/h over 0.60→0.73.
>
> **The selection factor does not cancel from `g_frac`** — the refuter's core
> structural claim survives intact. It cancels neither in form (different
> weightings: conditional-Gaussian vs φ) nor in effect (0 vs +207 nats/h).
>
> **This verdict is derivation-grade, not measurement-grade.** It must not be
> implemented in production before the two-venue counterfactual of §6, because
> the isolated form is exactly what ledger #66 measured as calibration-degrading
> in a 1D harness and #67 measured as *necessary but insufficient without its
> σ-model companion*. Claim-file caveat CC-1 binds.

