## 6. If the author rules DEFECT: the proposed route (measurement first, gate second)

**Order is binding** (research-cycle rule 6, measurement-before-gate; and claim
caveat CC-1): the counterfactual runs **before** any `/physics-change` package is
presented for approval, not after.

### 6.1 Counterfactual toggle — instrumentation, default-off

Modelled on `--freeze_g_frac_ref_h` (commits `930a9484`, `c917ed87`), which is the
precedent for "add an instrument, change nothing by default, read the
counterfactual".

```
--selection_in_completion_numerator {off,1d,both}     default: off
```

* `off` — **bit-identical to `main`**. Regression: byte-compare
  `event_likelihoods.csv` against the run of record.
* `1d` — multiply `completion_numerator_integrand` (`:4096`) by
  `S̄_φ(z;h)` interpolated on the existing `precompute_phi_marginal_survival`
  table (`:1782-1830` — **no new physics object is introduced**; the table is
  already built every run for `β^φ`). The 2D companion at `:4147` multiplies by
  the same `S̄_φ` **only** if the author also wants the naive symmetric variant;
  the derived form for `both` is (T1′).
* `both` — additionally carry `S_4D(d_L(z;h), x_M·M_z,det)` **inside** the
  Gauss–Hermite loop of `completion_mass_factor_g` (`:1987-1995`), i.e. the
  literal (T1′). Expected to be numerically ≈ `off` for the 2D channel; this cell
  exists to *measure* that expectation (M2), not to assume it.

Emitted diagnostics per event per h: `S_bar_phi_at_quadrature_peak`,
`delta_ln_B_num`, `delta_ln_B_num_wbh`, `delta_ln_g_frac`. Tag: `instrumentation`
(plain GSD), **not** `formula` — the default path is unchanged, so no
`/physics-change` gate is required to *build* it. The gate is required only to
change the default.

### 6.2 The two-venue 41-h counterfactual

Venues: `iiib` (idealized) and `joint_r1` (realistic) — the same pair gate (vii)
and the frozen-g run used, so the comparison is against bit-identical survivor
sets. Grid: canonical 41 points [0.60, 0.86]. Cells: `off` (control, must
reproduce the run of record exactly), `1d`, `both`.

### 6.3 Pre-registration skeleton (bands to be fixed BEFORE running; append-only)

| read | prediction | band |
|---|---|---|
| **P-1** control fidelity | `off` reproduces `run_20260804_postfix` | bit-identical `event_likelihoods.csv`; **any** difference invalidates the run |
| **P-2** 1D tilt magnitude | `Σ_i Δln p_i^{1D}` over 0.60→0.86 matches the §4 forecast | **+207 ± 40 nats/h** (the ±20% band covers the point-GW approximation and the completion-share hole, claim C6 hole (ii)) |
| **P-3** 1D sign/coherence | fraction of events with positive `Δ`-slope | **≥ 0.90** (forecast 0.947) |
| **P-4** 2D inertness | `Σ_i Δln p_i^{2D}` in cell `both` | **\|Σ\| ≤ 20 nats/h** ⇒ §3.1 CONFIRMED. `> 20` ⇒ the `σ_cond`/tail argument fails and the 2D verdict flips to defect |
| **P-5** `g_frac` residual | `Σ Δln g_frac` | **−207 ± 40 nats/h**, i.e. residual slope `+36 ± 40` — a band that **includes zero**; a zero-consistent residual is a *first-class recorded outcome*, not a success criterion |
| **P-6** 1D MAP | reported, **not** pre-banded | the never-add-MAP rule forbids predicting it from P-2; record it and stop |
| **P-7** 2D MAP | reported | expected unmoved if P-4 holds |
| **P-8 — Mixed branch (first-class)** | P-2 in band **and** P-4 out of band, or vice versa | report the split; do **not** force a branch. Route to M2 |
| **P-9 — expected NULL** | the `--freeze_g_frac_ref_h` frozen-g objects and the 1D *selection* objects (`β^φ`, `D̃^φ`, `Σ⁴ᴰ`) | **unchanged**; a move means the toggle leaked into the normalisation and the run is void |
| **P-10 — #66 pairing probe** | CC-1's open question | record whether the corrected 1D channel's coverage improves or degrades in the `pp_coverage` harness once that harness has a mass channel. **Explicitly deferred** — the harness gap is TO-BUILD (`research-cycle/SKILL.md:135-143`) |

